          "name": "page_to_markdown",
          "canonical_hash": "sha256:006cadf3fbc2178e7b1bdc76da8fe0ce7584c746f5797f1d1091825e7a3e1f3a",
          "description": "Fetch a web page URL and convert it to clean Markdown optimized for LLM context. Preserves headings, code blocks (with language hints), links, and tables; keeps the main content and drops navigation, headers, footers, and sidebars. It fetches without cookies and runs no page scripts, so a page behind a sign-in or one rendered only by JavaScript comes back as its login page or with no content; read those through a browser tool instead. It requests only the URL given, as a browser opens a page, so docs sites return the page itself, not a Markdown copy of it; a URL that names a Markdown or text file (a raw GitHub README.md, an llms.txt) comes back as written. Discovers tab groups statically and emits each panel as a",
